ck  okay and i'll come on to those plans a  little bit later but i'm talking about  right now you mentioned that meeting  yesterday with boris johnson and some of  the energy chiefs but they weren't all  there were they some of the big players  weren't there bp and shell weren't there  at the end of it no announcement no  action taken so what was the point of it  was it all about being seen to be doing  something i think it's recognizing that  of course uh uh what people rely on in  terms of uh some of the changes that may  need to be made it's important that the  prime minister the chancellor and the  energy secretary have those direct  conversations  um it's uh i'm very conscious of the  ongoing investment that still needs to  be made in the energy industry  in order to help us move towards net  zero in the future but understandably  right now some of our challenges are  global uh but some of our challenges we  need to make sure we increase the energy  security and resilience of this country  so we're not reliant  on just uh what was happening to world  gas prices  but also further changes that may be  needed in the market and the regulation  as well well yes i'm sure they're  important discussions that are being had  but don't people deserve to know now  whether or not they're going to be  facing higher bills with with no support  in the autumn i mean a lot of people are  very anxious and very stressed some of  the most vulnerable people people that  you represent as uh work and pensions um  secretary don't they need to have some  action spelled out now  well we have already set in place i took  legislation through parliament in june  and we've already started making those  payments every household will be getting  support next month toward their cost of  their bills well i'm conscious that uh  people may are seeing these numbers in  the news um offgem is uh due to report  at the end of this month i think it's  important to say government is working  already to c